"""Where the November 2026 rewrite moved the prose under check_paper_numbers.py's registered claims.

The rewrite for the ICLR 2027 discussion period cut the body and appendix by about half and reworded
most surviving sentences, so 145 of the registry's patterns stopped matching the sites they were
written for. Each was classified against the submitted text (commit 3f01124) and the current one:

  REANCHORED  the sentence survives in new wording; the pattern follows it. "order" maps the new
              capture groups onto the registered expected values when the clause order changed.
  LOWERED     the canonical site survives but restatements were cut; min_sites drops to what exists.
  RETIRED     the sentence, or the number in it, is no longer in the paper. The reason says which.

Nothing here changes an expected value: every value still comes from rederive(), so a re-anchored
pattern that lands on a wrong number fails exactly as before.
"""

